{#
  /happy-hour/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.

  This page earns 1,361 clicks with ZERO internal links pointing at it. It
  catches 1,107 happy-hour clicks across 165 queries; all six location pages
  combined catch 32, because "tajima happy hour" contains no location and a
  location page cannot answer it. It is now linked from the footer, /menu/,
  and the Convoy address plate.

  Per Steve, it stays OUT of the header nav tonight. Adding a fifth item to a
  header signed off with four is a design decision, not a build one.

  ============================ TIMES AND PRICES ARE PULLED ============================

  This page previously rendered per-location windows (11:30am to 6:00pm, and
  Convoy's late-night Fri/Sat) plus drink and food prices, all carried from the
  design concept. They were removed on Steve's call and the reasoning is the
  same one that keeps opening hours off every other page: CLIENT_FACTS.md
  forbids publishing hours the door does not honor, a happy hour window is the
  same promise, and the failure mode is someone driving over at 5 for a window
  that shut at 4. The prices were worse: CLAUDE.md says menu prices are never
  published without client approval and nobody at Tajima has seen these.

  The markup for windows, drinks, and food is still below, behind an `if`.
  Populate _data/happyHour.json with real values from Amanda and it renders
  again. Do not restore the concept values.

  WHAT SURVIVES IS ONLY WHAT TRACES TO CLIENT_FACTS.md:
    - happy hour exists and varies by room
    - Plaza Bonita is quick-serve with no alcohol, so it has none
    - East Village runs Padres game-night beer specials and longer hours on
      home game nights. EAST VILLAGE ONLY. Not widened to the other rooms, and
      the concept's "$3.50 every tap beer, all locations" is gone with the rest.
#}

<section class="hh-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="hh-hero__inner">
    <span class="hh-hero__eyebrow">San Diego</span>
    <h1 class="hh-hero__title" id="page-title">Happy Hour</h1>
    <p class="hh-hero__sub">
      Happy hour runs at most of the San Diego rooms, and the window is not the same everywhere. We are confirming the current times room by room. Until they are up here, call the one you are heading to and they will tell you. <a href="/locations/">Find your Tajima</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{#
  ============ SELECTOR REMOVED, CARDS REPLACED WITH A FACTS LIST ============
  2026-08-05.

  This was a six-pill jump nav over a three-column card grid. Five of the six
  rooms have no confirmed happy hour data, so the selector's entire function
  was to scroll you to a card reading "Times are being confirmed." A filter
  over mostly-empty data adds interface without adding information.

  What replaces it states each room's status directly, in one pass, in the
  order the rooms appear everywhere else on the site. No pills, no anchors,
  nothing to operate.

  THE CONDITIONAL IS UNCHANGED AND DELIBERATE. Each row still branches three
  ways: no alcohol, confirmed windows, or pending. The windows / drinks / food
  markup is intact, so the moment Amanda sends real values into
  _data/happyHour.json those rooms render their times here with no template
  change. This is a presentation change, not a capability removal.
#}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="confirmed-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <span class="sect__eyebrow">Room by room</span>
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="confirmed-title">What we can <em>confirm.</em></h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        Two things are settled and the rest are being checked. Where a time is not up here yet, the room's number is, and they will tell you what is running today.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ul class="hh-facts">
      {%- for hh in happyHour.locations %}
      {%- set loc = (locations.items | where("id", hh.id)) | first %}
      <li class="hh-facts__row">
        <div class="hh-facts__who">
          <h3 class="hh-facts__name"><a href="{{ loc.url }}">{{ hh.name }}</a></h3>
          <span class="hh-facts__tag">{{ hh.tag }}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hh-facts__state">
          {%- if hh.noAlcohol %}
          {#
            Confirmed in CLIENT_FACTS.md. Stated outright rather than left as a
            gap for someone to drive to National City and discover.
          #}
          <p class="hh-facts__no">No happy hour here. Quick-serve inside the mall, and no alcohol. The bowls are the same bowls.</p>

          {%- elif hh.windows | length %}
          {# Renders only when happyHour.json holds confirmed values. #}
          <div class="hh-facts__hours">
            {%- for window in hh.windows %}
            <div class="hh-facts__hours-row">
              <span>{{ window.time }}</span>
              <span class="hh-facts__days">{{ window.days }}</span>
            </div>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          {%- if hh.drinks | length or hh.food | length %}
          <div class="hh-facts__lists">
            {%- if hh.drinks | length %}
            <div>
              <p class="hh-facts__list-label">Drinks</p>
              <ul class="hh-facts__list">
                {%- for item in hh.drinks %}<li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>{% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </div>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if hh.food | length %}
            <div>
              <p class="hh-facts__list-label">Food</p>
              <ul class="hh-facts__list">
                {%- for item in hh.food %}<li><span>{{ item.name }}</span><span>{{ item.price }}</span></li>{% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </div>
            {%- endif %}
          </div>
          {%- endif %}

          {%- else %}
          <p class="hh-facts__pending">Times are being confirmed.</p>
          <a class="hh-facts__phone" href="tel:+1-{{ loc.phone | replace('(', '') | replace(') ', '-') | replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ loc.phone }}</a>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

